      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vertical scaling involves enhancing the capacity of a single server, such as by upgrading its RAM or processor, to handle increased demands. In contrast, horizontal scaling expands system capacity by adding multiple servers to work together, allowing for greater fault tolerance and flexibility. For your stakeholders, choosing between these approaches depends largely on whether your goal is a targeted performance boost on existing hardware or a robust expansion to support future growth. This distinction ensures you allocate resources efficiently while maintaining reliability during our upcoming infrastructure changes.",
